Hardly.  Knights get a very good artifact faster than any other class.  Very
handy for the mines.  Also, when engraving
that spear never gets dull; not as good as an asthame, but the next best thing.
They start with decent weaponry and armor, as well as a very usefull intrinsic
for getting out of those tight spots.

Now, those archeologists, they truely reek.  Pick-axe?  Bah!  They are easy
to find these days.  Food?  Bah!  Just eat all those (`safe') corpses.
Identify gems?  Bah!  Need money?  Identify the white gems at the bottom of 
the mines.  Intrinsic searching?  Bah!  Just wield excalibur (if your a knight).
They get hurt by falling rocks (fedora is worthless, tho quite fashionable I 
hear - knights, BTW,  start with a helm), start with the worst starting weapon 
in the game (well, ok maybe the scalple is worse - barely).  No non-lawful
monsters in the mines have decent armor (dwarves are lawful).  I've had to
go forever with starting armor.  They have nothing and are of the most 
useless alignment.

Knights one on one can overpower any (hostile) critter they reach early in 
the game, excluding those polymorph trap creations, purple worms (never 
happened to me),
etc.  Arcs can't say that.  I've had to run from goblins with these guys.
I think they should start with at least a missle weapon (like knights).  My
second ascention was with a knight.  I can't for the life of me get an arc
past the mines.

Why can't we have a class that starts with nothing?  No armor.  No weapon.
No inventory whatsoever.  On top of that, no god as a mentor (in other words,
they can't pray).  They would have to find an altar to gain alignment (first
prayer at an altar should convert - they would have 0 alignment at that point).
Give them no intrinsics and a pet mouse for starters (grows to a giant rat
eventually if it never gets hit).  This would be a true guru class.  Class
name could be guru (named after the player that first ascends with one).
Character stats, of course, would be 100% random (3d6).  Quest item?  How 
about a coka-cola bottle (from the movie `the gods must be crazy')?  It would
give you intrinsic agravate-familiar (just like the movie).  In all fairness,
the coka-cola bottle should be non-wishable and worthless except being worth
tons of points (to make sure they get all the top scores).
